# Cyrius Field Notes — Compiler Internal Gotchas
# Non-obvious traps an agent will hit when working on cyrius's
# compiler internals: regalloc, layout, alignment, IR ordering,
# heap caps, fn-table conventions, codegen-vs-IR divergence.
#
# Earn their slot when an agent is debugging a cyrius
# regression that doesn't fit a clean pattern. The shape is
# always "this surprised future-me; here's the diagnosis +
# fix + how to recognize it again."
#
# For process methodology see methodology.cyml.
# For design patterns see patterns.cyml.
# For full backstory + chronological context see retros/.
#
# ⚠ `vr01_` IN OLDER ENTRIES IS A HISTORICAL FILENAME, NOT AN INSTRUCTION. That prefix
#   selected the cross-OS corpus until v6.5.11; the selector is now the
#   `tests/tcyr/crossos/` DIRECTORY and zero `vr01_*` files remain. Naming a new test
#   `vr01_*` today opts it OUT of the release gate's cross-OS leg — the opposite of what
#   the prefix used to mean. Live paths were repaired at the v6.6.1 audit; remaining
#   mentions are inside narratives about bugs found when the file was called that.
#
# 105 entries (v6.6.1 — an AUDIT. The count went DOWN.)
#
#   ⛔ THIS FILE WAS APPEND-ONLY FOR TOO LONG. It reached **158 entries / 5,566 lines /
#   461 KB** — a volume nobody searches, which defeats the whole point: a gotchas file
#   you will not read is worth LESS than none, because it still costs a lookup and
#   returns noise. The v6.6.1 pass added 5 for the v6.6.x band and then cut hard:
#
#     158 → 149  · 13 entries merged into 4. Four clusters were ONE lesson each, split
#                  across releases: the v6.5.50/.51 "confidently-named wrong cause",
#                  inline-replay + SIMD residency, gate/mutation proof discipline, and
#                  install.sh copy semantics.
#     149 → 105  · 44 entries moved to `retros/resolved_traps.cyml` — ARCHIVED, not
#                  deleted. They were one of two things, and neither is a live trap:
#                  a specific bug in a specific release whose code has since been
#                  restructured (the v5.11.x kernel/PE/EFI cluster, the Mach-O
#                  byte-array fixes, the aarch64 epoll reactor), or a CHANGE RECORD
#                  wearing a gotcha's clothes ("v6.3.8 added lexical capture",
#                  "v6.4.51 raised output_buf to 1 GiB").
#
#   Also fixed: 4 entries carrying ~500 lines of v5.11.x BACKSTORY compressed to the
#   trap plus a pointer (`retros/v511x.cyml` already held the narrative); 1 entry that
#   was FACTUALLY WRONG IN ITS OWN NAME (it asserted the reserved-token count is "67
#   not 51"; the live count is 76 — three values for one set, in three files); 1
#   pre-existing syntax defect (a stray closing triple-quote from an old `content=` →
#   `---` conversion); and 12 dead test paths (`tests/tcyr/vr01_X.tcyr` →
#   `tests/tcyr/crossos/X.tcyr`).
#
#   Net: **158 → 105 entries, 5,566 → 3410 lines.**
#
#   ⭐ THE ADMISSION RULE, because this file will regrow otherwise. An entry earns a
#   slot ONLY if it can still bite someone working on cyrius today. Before adding:
#     · Is it a trap, or a change record? A change record goes to the CHANGELOG and to
#       `language/features.cyml`.
#     · Is an existing entry the same lesson wearing a different release number? Merge.
#     · Is it over ~40 lines? The narrative belongs in `retros/`; only the TRAP here.
#     · Is it now impossible — hard-errored, gated, or the code path removed? Then it
#       belongs in `retros/resolved_traps.cyml`, not here.
#
#   Live state at 6.6.1: cycc x86_64 **1,247,608 B** (.text 1,090,832) · seed **29,024 B**
#   · check.sh **240 passed / 0 failed** · **144** shell gates · **301** .tcyr (68 crossos)
#   · **102** lib/*.cyr · api-surface **5152** · heap map **102** regions (gate-derived;
#   a raw grep says 145 by also matching FREED markers) · self_compile **731-734 ms** ·
#   **0** open issues · cross-OS SELFHOST_OK + crossos LIBTEST_OK on ecb/ach/cass/pi.
#
# 149 entries (v6.5.56 — +1 on invariants that silently carry other properties; earlier: 148 at v6.5.55 — +1 on value-vs-lifetime for sum types; earlier: 147 at v6.5.54 — +2 on mutation-proof integrity and stale perf numbers; earlier: 140 at v6.5.51 — +3 covering the .51 compile-time root-cause. Count re-derived by
#   `grep -c '^\[\[entries\]\]'`, not incremented from the line below. The through-line of the
#   block: **all three are about a cause that was CONFIDENTLY NAMED and wrong.** cycc's
#   compile-time superlinearity was blamed on `_fnt_grow` for a whole release (it costs 4-9 ms
#   across an entire 120,000-fn compile, not the 1145 ms attributed to a single call), on a
#   rehash that doubles and is therefore amortized-linear by construction, and on a DCE walk
#   that is OFF by default and never ran in any measurement — while the real cause was an
#   open-addressed hash grown only when FULL, quadratic by construction, sitting in two
#   innocuous lines in different files. Separately, a manifest feature shipped inert for 96 %
#   of consumers because its key was read from THIS repo instead of counted across theirs, and
#   its gate agreed because the gate was written alongside the implementation. The habit that
#   catches all three is the one .50's block already named: instrument or count the thing
#   itself before designing around a stated mechanism. Live state at 6.5.51:
#   cycc x86_64 **1,192,312 B** (.text 1,042,416) · seed **29,024 B** (seed→cybs→cycc
#   byte-identical) · check.sh **236 passed / 0 failed** · **119** shell gates in `tests/gates/`
#   (DERIVED, never hand-incremented) · self_compile **661.8 ms** — under the ≤700 ms cap; deliberately
#   FLAT vs .50 because cycc's own ~1,251 fns never entered the saturation band .51 fixes · cross-OS SELFHOST_OK + crossos LIBTEST_OK on ecb / ach / cass / pi, real
#   hardware.)
#
