# 82 entries (v6.4.44, Win64 retptr deep-stack-param homing: +1 gotcha
# win64_retptr_shifted_deep_stack_param_homing_offbyone_prologue_postloop_missing_pp_shift_f32v8_make_lanes_567
# — a value-form-SIMD/struct-returning fn on Win64 PE (hidden retptr in RCX) with >6 params homed its
# DEEP stack params (pidx>=6, the post-loop at parse_fn.cyr ~3404) one local slot too deep and dropped
# the last, because the post-loop used the param index as BOTH source ABI slot AND dest local slot with
# NO retptr shift — while the IN-loop homing (~3321) DOES apply `_pp_shift` and the body reads the
# contiguous -0x30-lidx*8 slots via FINDLOCAL. f32v8_make(a..h) lanes 5,6,7 = garbage on cass, 0-4 OK;
# Linux/SysV fine (no retptr for SIMD register returns, so _pl_shift==0 == old code == byte-id). Fix:
# mirror _pp_shift in the post-loop (pidx=spi+shift src, lidx=spi dest, start spi=6-shift). Pre-existing
# since v6.4.31; latent bc vr01_f32v8_ctor's stale "skips cass" comment masked that CYRIUS_HAS_VAL_SIMD_
# PARAMS went true on PE at .31. Root-caused by disassembling caller (correct) vs callee prologue (skew).)
# 81 entries (v6.4.44, PE reroute 16-align: +1 gotcha
# pe_kernel32_reroutes_fixed_sub_rsp_only_aligns_on_right_parity_closehandle_faults_on_misalign_wine_cannot_repro
# — 8 PE kernel32 reroutes (ECLOSE_PE/EWAIT/EGETEXIT/ESETHANDLE/ECREATEPIPE/EGETCMDLINE/EGETTICKS/EMMAP)
# used a FIXED `sub rsp,0x28` that only 16-aligns the call when the caller's rsp lands on the right
# parity; CloseHandle faults 0xC0000005 on an aligned SSE access inside kernel32 when misaligned.
# Exposed by the async subprocess resume (deep call stack): 2 sequential async_run_process crashed,
# single+batched worked (parity-dependent). CreateProcessW was fixed this way at v6.0.51 but its comment
# wrongly generalized "≤4-arg reroutes tolerate a misalign". Fix: route through the rbx-anchored
# _pe_call_Narg_aligned / _pe_srw_call_1arg helpers. WINE aligns leniently → returned 42 throughout;
# only real Windows repros. WriteFile-trace of _async_step localized it after ckA/ckR/ckG bisection.)
# 79 entries (v6.4.32, cx SIMD codegen: +1 gotcha
# cx_simd_emitters_are_easy_the_real_bugs_are_local_addressing_eloadlocaladdr_stub_and_regalloc_disp_nonuniformity
# — cx SIMD emitters mirror the f64 loop trivially; the real blockers are 2 pre-existing cx
# local-addressing bugs the SIMD pointer-stash exposes (ELOAD_LOCAL_ADDR return-0 stub → &local
# aliases addr 0; scalar load/store disp omitted the regalloc/ret_stash reservation EFLADDR had →
# stash collides with arrays; unify via _cx_ldisp). cxvm >> is LOGICAL (dp8 sign-ext = b−((b>>7)<<8)).
# git-stash-rebuild-vs-baseline proves regression-vs-pre-existing; end cx gates with `return assert_summary()`.)
# 78 entries (v6.4.28, SIMD Phase 5 f32v4 NEON: +1 gotcha
# aarch64_neon_simd_emitter_mirror_f64v_loop_verify_encodings_with_llvm_mc_and_value_form_params_die_on_win64
# — a new aarch64 NEON SIMD emitter (EMIT_F32V_*) mirrors the existing EMIT_F64V_LOOP/DOT (change
# .2d→.4s, lsl#3→lsl#2, +2→+4); verify every hand-encoded word with `llvm-mc --show-encoding`;
# match x86 rounding (fmul+fadd, NOT fused fmla) for fmadd/dot; DON'T make a value-form SIMD test a
# full vr01_ — value-form f32v4 params hard-error on Win64 PE, so gate the flat-array subset instead.)
# 77 entries (v6.4.27, agnos O_RDWR flag-map: +1 gotcha
# agnos_ao_access_mode_bits_are_1to1_with_linux_o_flags_pass_through_dont_fold_verify_under_mirshi
# — agnos AO_RDONLY/WRONLY/RDWR = 0/1/2 == Linux O_*; io.cyr:80 folded (flags&3)!=0 → |0x1 so
# O_RDWR became write-only and reads failed on agnos ONLY; fold passed compile+Linux, only mirshi
# read-after-write caught it; fix `ao |= flags&3`; the sakshi.cyr dup is a fold → fix at source.)
# 76 entries (v6.4.26, Windows PE batch: +1 gotcha
# new_pe_reroute_fn_needs_return0_stubs_in_aarch64_and_cx_backends_for_symbol_resolution
# — a new E*_PE reroute fn (real impl in backend/x86/emit.cyr) called from parse_expr.cyr is
# referenced by ALL forks; aarch64/cx/macho backends need a `fn X_PE(S){return 0;}` stub or
# the cx/aarch64 cycc build fails "undefined function" — invisible to local Linux+wine tests
