# 75 entries (v6.4.25, aarch64 exp2/atan + Payne-Hanek: +1 gotcha
# aarch64_transcendental_polyfill_dispatch_and_dekker_dd_range_reduction
# — aarch64 has no native exp2/atan/trig; EF64_* route to lib/math.cyr _f64_*_polyfill via
# _FINDFN_CSTR; large-|x| trig needs a NO-FMA Dekker double-double reduction, gated so the
# small-angle path stays byte-identical; lib/math.cyr is NOT in cycc so x86 stays byte-id.)
# 74 entries (v6.4.24, P1 struct-field: +1 gotcha
# struct_field_access_mis_parsed_as_enum_variant_when_field_name_shadows_a_global_var
# — X.Y disambiguation loaded a global whenever the FIELD name was a global var, ignoring
# base X; fix = if X is a known var, X.Y is a field access (enum-variant base is a TYPE).)
# 73 entries (v6.4.21, LEXID cap: +1 gotcha
# heap_region_shared_by_all_forks_must_relocate_to_arena_top_because_fork_arenas_diverge
# — growing a fixed-offset heap region a SHARED file touches means relocating to the
# arena top + extending ALL 7 forks' arenas (they map DIFFERENT sizes: x86/win 0x7300000
# with the IR arena, aarch64/macho/cx only 0x5E1D000); lazy mmap makes the extra range free.)
# 72 entries (v6.4.20, cx arc C: +1 gotcha
# cxvm_guest_syscall_is_compiler_renumbered_at_runtime_fix_pointer_slot_and_pe_arity
# — a portable .cyx runs cross-OS via a cxvm-ONLY fix: the compiler already
# renumbers a runtime var syscall number per-host (ESYSXLAT/EMACHO), so the bugs
# were the open pointer-slot (s2 not s3) + the Windows argc-6 arity-bucket miss
# (→ arity-correct dispatch); cycc_cx cross-compiles clean but faults on macOS.)
# 71 entries (v6.4.10, 6.4.x SIMD arc: +2 gotchas from the v6.4.4-.10
# SIMD-compute-arc + fixes work — vex_encoding_vvvv_ones_complement_and_fma_cpuid_leaf
# (the FIRST VEX/AVX the toolchain emits: the VEX vvvv field is the 1's-COMPLEMENT
# of src1 → a wrong-polarity nibble assembles VALID but reads the WRONG register,
# invisible to self-host → disasm-gate every new VEX op; FMA is CPUID leaf 1 ECX.12,
# a DIFFERENT leaf+bit than AVX2's leaf 7 EBX.5) and
# two_step_bootstrap_for_toplevel_array_sizing_and_legit_codegen_diff (a change to
# how cycc sizes its OWN top-level arrays is a TWO-STEP bootstrap, same class as
# W^X-flip; and a real bug fix SHOULD show differential codegen-diff>0 WITH
# status-diff=0 — codegen-diff=0 on a behavior fix means it didn't fire).)
# 68 entries (v6.4.2, 6.4.x: +2 gotchas from the v6.4.0/.1 generics-flip +
# allocator-hardening work — monomorph_default_on_flip_gftp_decouple
# (CYRIUS_MONOMORPH default-on needed GFTP(S,fi)!=0 as the precise per-fn
# signal + decoupling from _INLINE_OK to avoid a +25.6% general-inlining
# regression; generics are now DEFAULT-ON, CYRIUS_MONOMORPH=0 opts out) and
# alloc_reset_zero_on_reset_chunk_model_and_lib_fix_not_auto_byte_identical
# (zero-on-reset info-leak fix; _heap_used is cumulative so a naive memset
# over-runs the first chunk; a lib fix is NOT auto cycc-byte-identical when
# cycc includes the lib).)
# 64 entries (v6.3.x closeout, 6.3.44: +4 durable gotchas from the .43/.44
# cross-OS + stdlib correctness sweep — macho_syscall_xlat_source_numbers_arch_specific
